WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.444
ALEX: So. Thirty-five billion
dollars in a single stock

00:00:02.444 --> 00:00:04.888
ALEX: offering. Meta filed this
today. Walk me through

00:00:04.888 --> 00:00:07.331
ALEX: the structure, because it
isn't just one big

00:00:07.331 --> 00:00:09.775
ALEX: pile of shares.

00:00:09.885 --> 00:00:13.153
RUFUS: Two tranches. About twenty-
two-and-a-half billion in Class A

00:00:13.153 --> 00:00:16.422
RUFUS: common stock — the regular
shares. And then

00:00:16.422 --> 00:00:19.690
RUFUS: another twelve-and-a-half
billion in depositary shares
representing mandatory

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:22.958
RUFUS: convertible preferred
stock.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.722
JAMIE: What's the preferred stock
doing there?

00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:28.498
RUFUS: Investors get a fixed
return for a period,

00:00:28.498 --> 00:00:31.189
RUFUS: then the shares
automatically convert into common
stock.

00:00:31.189 --> 00:00:33.879
RUFUS: It lets Meta attract people
who want a

00:00:33.879 --> 00:00:36.570
RUFUS: bit more downside
protection without issuing bonds.
